     "id": "notes-1",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "- **Purpose.** Persistence in one picture: the coefficient on the lag is the share of a shock carried into the next period, so the response to a one-time shock is $\\beta_1^k\\varepsilon$. At $\\beta_1 = 1$ (a unit root) shocks are permanent and the series has no mean to return to — it is not stationary. The bottom panel is the impulse response a [Vector Autoregression](note:vector-autoregression) reports, for the one-variable case.\n- **Model.** A view of [AR(1) Process Model](note:ar-1-process-model).\n- **Elements.** Panels `level` (series `series`, `mean`) and `irf` (series `response`). Readouts `after4_out`, `share10_out`.\n- **Tests.** Python."
      }
     ],
     "words": 93,
     "symbols": [
      "$\\beta_0$",
      "$\\varepsilon_t$",
      "$s$, $k$"
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
